      "title": "Setup and selection behaviour",
      "properties": {
        "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "# Smart selection with native WeVisOne\n\nChoose an image and install/select wevisone_vl_2b_int8_convrot.safetensors from Comfy-Org/WeVisOne-VL. CLIPLoader uses stable_diffusion as its type: current core auto-detects the WeVisOne architecture from the weights. This is a perception model, not the generator's text encoder.\n\nSmart Select can select face, person, hair or other descriptions. Segmentation returns alpha mattes; detection returns rectangular masks. Largest selects one match per image. Index uses the native detector's zero-based order; inspect the report when several subjects match. All keeps every match. No match yields an empty mask and no boxes; Region Crop stops rather than silently refining the whole image.\n\nMask Editor lets you correct the incoming selection after a first run. A saved painting overrides the incoming mask until Use input mask is clicked. Clear saves an all-black painting. If painting outside a selected box, disconnect the boxes from Region Crop to derive the crop bounds from the edited mask instead.\n\n# Face-region refinement\n\nSelect a Flux.2 reference bundle and matching Klein Base 4B components, including the matching VAE. The original scene prompt guides refinement. The selected face is padded and enlarged to a 768-pixel long edge on a 16-pixel grid. Its VAE-encoded pixels feed the sampler; references remain active throughout. The whole padded crop is sampled. The soft selection mask is applied only at pasteback: using that fractional matte as a latent noise mask repeatedly suppresses changes during sampling. Denoise 0.20 is a conservative redraw, not guaranteed restoration. Compare the crop at working resolution. 0.35 produces stronger changes but can alter facial features or tattoo details.\n\nRegion Composite restores the crop's original size and blends it into the SAME original source image. The output stays at the source image's resolution. Only the chosen frame/region is changed; other pixels and alpha are preserved. Use an enlarged input first if you also want the whole output at a higher resolution. Inspect the mask, crop and before/after comparison; face detection is not identity recognition and refinement cannot guarantee exact identity."
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
        "text": "# Smart selection with native WeVisOne\n\nChoose an image and install/select wevisone_vl_2b_int8_convrot.safetensors from Comfy-Org/WeVisOne-VL. CLIPLoader uses stable_diffusion as its type: current core auto-detects the WeVisOne architecture from the weights. This is a perception model, not the generator's text encoder.\n\nSmart Select can select face, person, hair or other descriptions. Segmentation returns alpha mattes; detection returns rectangular masks. Largest selects one match per image. Index uses the native detector's zero-based order; inspect the report when several subjects match. All keeps every match. No match yields an empty mask and no boxes; Region Crop stops rather than silently refining the whole image.\n\nMask Editor lets you correct the incoming selection after a first run. A saved painting overrides the incoming mask until Use input mask is clicked. Clear saves an all-black painting. If painting outside a selected box, disconnect the boxes from Region Crop to derive the crop bounds from the edited mask instead.\n\n# Face-region refinement\n\nSelect a Flux.2 reference bundle and matching Klein Base 4B components, including the matching VAE. The original scene prompt guides refinement. The selected face is padded and enlarged to a 768-pixel long edge on a 16-pixel grid. Its VAE-encoded pixels feed the sampler; references remain active throughout. The whole padded crop is sampled. The soft selection mask is applied only at pasteback: using that fractional matte as a latent noise mask repeatedly suppresses changes during sampling. Denoise 0.20 is a conservative redraw, not guaranteed restoration. Compare the crop at working resolution. 0.35 produces stronger changes but can alter facial features or tattoo details.\n\nRegion Composite restores the crop's original size and blends it into the SAME original source image. The output stays at the source image's resolution. Only the chosen frame/region is changed; other pixels and alpha are preserved. Use an enlarged input first if you also want the whole output at a higher resolution. Inspect the mask, crop and before/after comparison; face detection is not identity recognition and refinement cannot guarantee exact identity."
      }
    },
